From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: airoha: publish a non-zero minimum timeout

airoha_wdt_probe() left wdog_dev->min_timeout at 0, allowing userspace to
set a 0-second timeout that loaded 0 ticks and reset the board immediately.
Set min_timeout = 1 so the watchdog core rejects zero timeouts with -EINVAL.

Origin: archive/xr1710g-v1@e85677d284c0
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/watchdog/airoha_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/airoha_wdt.c
@@ -159,6 +159,8 @@ static int airoha_wdt_probe(struct platf
 	wdog_dev->ops = &airoha_wdt_ops;
 	/* Bus 300MHz, watchdog 150MHz, 28 seconds */
 	wdog_dev->max_timeout = FIELD_MAX(WDT_TIMER_VAL) / airoha_wdt->wdt_freq;
+	/* A zero-tick load value resets the board on the next tick */
+	wdog_dev->min_timeout = 1;
 	wdog_dev->parent = dev;
 
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(wdog_dev, airoha_wdt);
